From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:34:42 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] x11window: Tell a window that declares stereo content the
 depth limits of its output

Stereo KWin sends kde_stereo_depth_v1.depth_limits to a Wayland surface that
asked for it. An X11 client cannot ask: its surface is Xwayland's, so the limits
of the output it sits on never reached it, and a program running in an X11
window (the OpenXR runtime's own window, a game, a toolkit) could not draw
inside the depth the person set for that screen.

StereoDepthStates::update() already has the two numbers for the window's
output. For an X11 window that declares stereo content it now also writes
them, as the Wayland event carries them (wl_fixed_t, 24.8 fixed point, pixels
of a view 1920 wide), in _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_DEPTH_LIMITS: CARDINAL/32, exactly
two values, sunk then popped. The property follows the person's settings, the
output's mode and kind and the window's move to another output, and goes when
the window stops declaring. _KDE_NET_WM_STEREO_CONTENT_SUPPORTED is 10, so a
client knows the property will come.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5 via Claude Code
